I believe I made the same damn mistake a very long time ago on nethack:
zapped the Wizard w/ cockatrice corpse.  Got very disheartened so I made
my way back to the entrance so that I would at least 'Escape From the Dun-
geon' with my bags of gems.  

It turned out that the Wizard ('Double Trouble!' to boot) ambushed me, as 
is his wont normally, very soon after I left Gehennom.  Since my character
was a priest sans magic resistance, he made short work of my goods/armor in
the first combat and slaughtered me not too long after that.  (Forgot exactly
how many times I fought him.)  The point is:  you MIGHT have a chance of
getting the Book of the Dead if the 'returning Wizard of Yendor' carries 
the book.  I died before I could find out.  

A friend of mine had a truly awesome character which had this happen to him:
one of the WoY's pets in the Wizard's lair was a black dragon.  You can 
easily guess what happened:  the dragon tried zapping him and hit the 
wizard.  Nothing left, including the book.  

So, instead of quitting, try seeing if the Wizard ambushes you.  It's 
worth a shot.  




